    "sensitive": false,
    "name": "Right-to-Left text support",
    "content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://author8.local/profile/omer\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>omer</span></a></span> wrote in a DM to the forum:</p><p>Hi,</p><p>I'm new to Friendica, and since I'm writing mostly in Hebrew, I wonder if the software can support Right-to-Left text directionality. Is that something that can be implemented on the server side? or even the user side? is there some kind of plugin or whatever?</p><p>Thanks,<br>Omer</p>",
    "contentMap": {
      "en": "<p><bdi>@<a href=\"https://author8.local/profile/omer\" class=\"userinfo mention\" title=\"omer\">omer</a></bdi> wrote in a DM to the forum:</p><p>Hi,</p><p>I'm new to Friendica, and since I'm writing mostly in Hebrew, I wonder if the software can support Right-to-Left text directionality. Is that something that can be implemented on the server side? or even the user side? is there some kind of plugin or whatever?</p><p>Thanks,<br>Omer</p>"
    },
    "source": {
      "content": "@[url=https://author8.local/profile/omer]Omer Ori[/url] wrote in a DM to the forum:\r\n\r\nHi,\r\n\r\nI'm new to Friendica, and since I'm writing mostly in Hebrew, I wonder if the software can support Right-to-Left text directionality. Is that something that can be implemented on the server side? or even the user side? is there some kind of plugin or whatever?\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nOmer",
